    {
      "id": "absolute-benefit-zh",
      "kind": "reader-summary-entry",
      "name": "Absolute versus relative benefit (number needed to treat) (zh)",
      "canonicalRecordId": "absolute-benefit",
      "language": "zh",
      "available": true,
      "text": "对于不良结局，绝对获益是在同一时间点用对照组风险减去治疗组风险；相对风险是治疗组风险除以对照组风险。这些群体指标不能指出谁会获益，也不能单独决定获益与伤害的权衡。"
    },
    {
      "id": "absolute-benefit-simple",
      "kind": "reader-summary-entry",
      "name": "Absolute versus relative benefit (number needed to treat) (simple)",
      "canonicalRecordId": "absolute-benefit",
      "language": "simple",
      "available": true,
      "text": "Absolute benefit is the difference in outcome chances between groups at a stated time; relative risk is their ratio. Neither measure says who benefits or settles the balance of benefit and harm."
    },
